WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.767
The query first prepares one revenue value per date.

00:00:03.767 --> 00:00:09.197
Then the window average uses the current row and up to two earlier rows.

00:00:09.197 --> 00:00:12.582
That creates a three-row moving average.

00:00:12.582 --> 00:00:19.607
Notice the phrase three-row. It does not automatically mean three calendar days.

00:00:19.607 --> 00:00:25.167
If some dates are missing, the three rows may cover a longer period of time.

00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:29.644
This is why the frame definition and the row grain both matter.
